cards.body:
The disaster: `UPDATE payments SET amount = 0;` — no WHERE clause. Every single payment in the table, zeroed, instantly, with no undo button.

An UPDATE or DELETE without a WHERE clause applies to EVERY row in the table. The **seatbelt**: always SELECT first, count what you're about to touch, THEN modify.

SELECT COUNT(*) FROM registrations WHERE session='2025/2026' AND grade IS NULL;
UPDATE registrations SET grade='F' WHERE session='2025/2026' AND grade IS NULL AND score < 40;

Same WHERE clause, run as a SELECT first. If that count surprises you — too big, too small — you just saved the table before doing anything irreversible.

The database version of the bank-app horror story everyone's heard at least once — a wrongly aimed transfer with no undo button, except this time it's an UPDATE with no WHERE clause instead of a fat-fingered account number.
